{"duration_api_ms":664763,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"34815b18-33f3-4435-be21-2ba5fa4fa9d7","total_cost_usd":2.8557979999999987,"usage":{"input_tokens":188,"cache_creation_input_tokens":117344,"cache_read_input_tokens":9519500,"output_tokens":47247,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":21291},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":117344,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3266,"cache_read_input_tokens":133468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":900},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9591,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009676,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":188,"outputTokens":47247,"cacheReadInputTokens":9519500,"cacheCreationInputTokens":117344,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.8461219999999985,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":21291,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":135,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured redundant L3 connectivity between node1's private network (node3) and node2's private network (node4) carried over both independent node1-node2 links, with automatic failover and full node-restart persistence verified on all four nodes.\\n\\nTopology discovery: node1 eth1/eth2 and node2 eth1/eth2 are the two independent uplinks between node1-node2; node1 eth3 connects to node3's enp8s0, node2 eth3 connects to node4's enp8s0 (confirmed via targeted ping tests, since interfaces carried no IPs initially).\\n\\nImplementation:\\n- node1: bond0 (Linux bonding, mode balance-rr, miimon 100) over eth1+eth2, IP 172.20.0.1/30 to node2; eth3 = 192.168.1.1/24 (node3's subnet). IP forwarding enabled globally and per-interface. Static route to 192.168.2.0/24 via bond0.\\n- node2: mirrored — bond0 172.20.0.2/30, eth3 = 192.168.2.1/24 (node4's subnet), route to 192.168.1.0/24 via bond0.\\n- node3/node4: enp8s0 statically addressed (192.168.1.2/24, 192.168.2.2/24) via existing NetworkManager profiles with a static route to the other private subnet via its local node1/node2 gateway — persists natively through NetworkManager.\\n- Persistence on node1/node2: a systemd oneshot unit (antrieb-links.service, enabled, WantedBy=multi-user.target) reapplies the bonding/IP/forwarding/route configuration at boot, since SONiC's interfaces-config.service only manages eth0/lo and does not touch eth1-3.\\n- Discovered and worked around a virtio/bonding limitation: 802.3ad (LACP) mode failed because virtio-net can't report link speed/duplex (dmesg: \\\"failed to get link speed/duplex\\\"), so switched to balance-rr, which works cleanly and actively load-balances across both links (confirmed via matched tx_packet counters growing symmetrically on eth1/eth2 for a test ping burst).\\n- Also discovered that the platform's virtual point-to-point links do not propagate one-sided admin-down to the peer's carrier state (verified: bringing node1's eth1 down did not clear LOWER_UP on node2's eth1), so failover was correctly demonstrated as a full link outage (both endpoints down), which is the realistic failure model — 0% packet loss for node3↔node4 traffic in that state, and clean automatic recovery once both ends were restored.\\n- Ran the mandatory node-restart protocol on all four nodes sequentially (one at a time, quorum/service preserved): captured pre-restart boot_id, restarted via `reboot`/`systemctl reboot`, polled until exec was available again, confirmed a new boot_id, and verified bonding/routes/forwarding/NetworkManager config and node3↔node4 connectivity recovered on each.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Mapped node1/node2/node3/node4 interface topology via targeted temporary-IP ping tests since interfaces carried no addresses\",\"Diagnosed and resolved a virtio-net + LACP (802.3ad) incompatibility, switching to balance-rr bonding\",\"Configured bond0 (balance-rr, miimon 100) on node1 and node2 spanning both independent uplinks\",\"Configured node1 eth3 (192.168.1.1/24) and node2 eth3 (192.168.2.1/24) as private-network gateways for node3/node4\",\"Enabled global and per-interface IPv4 forwarding on node1 and node2\",\"Added static routes on node1, node2, node3, node4 to reach the opposite private subnet\",\"Persisted node3/node4 static addressing and routes via existing NetworkManager 'Wired connection 2' profiles\",\"Created and enabled a systemd oneshot unit (antrieb-links.service) on node1 and node2 to reapply bonding/IP/forwarding/route config at boot\",\"Verified active-active use of both links via symmetric tx_packet counters on eth1/eth2 during a ping burst\",\"Disrupted link A (eth1) at both node1 and node2 to simulate a full link outage, confirmed 0% packet loss for node3<->node4 traffic, then restored and confirmed recovery and renewed dual-link usage\",\"Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on node1, node2, node3, and node4 sequentially: captured baseline boot_id, restarted, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified recovered bonding/network/connectivity state\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Traffic between node3 and node4 private networks carried over both node1-node2 links (active-active)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0f843b275ff9425e\",\"cmd-1252471645d7456b\",\"cmd-c76cc7515bdd4590\",\"cmd-610925e0415c4841\",\"cmd-abd4b358ffe34674\",\"cmd-f731b1ef61dd4c3c\"],\"summary\":\"bond0 (balance-rr) established on node1/node2 over eth1+eth2; node3->node4 ping succeeds; tx_packets on eth1 and eth2 both incremented by 23 during a 40-packet burst, proving both links carry traffic\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3/node4 keep reaching each other when either link is taken out of service\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e4a7ab7dcedf406c\",\"cmd-909eb0d3d5754798\",\"cmd-c6a273fd271e4464\",\"cmd-3e184f6642cd406f\",\"cmd-aca6c570f9b849c8\",\"cmd-5eb47c2c6e6b4c7a\",\"cmd-c08de683c1294324\",\"cmd-124486a0a16c4d4e\",\"cmd-6ba16d7d0ffe445b\",\"cmd-cae1127468c241b9\",\"cmd-732ea34c97a245f5\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline 0% loss; link A (eth1) disabled at both endpoints (realistic full-link-outage model, since platform links don't propagate one-sided down); node3->node4 ping showed 0% loss over remaining link B; link A restored, bond returned to MII up on both slaves, and both links resumed carrying traffic evenly\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart persistence and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1fe7c86cc22a44f7\",\"cmd-c116ca98add84f07\",\"cmd-6a02d7168c6a48d9\",\"cmd-d86b112ab0734c15\",\"cmd-9d790d98a75e4e89\",\"cmd-dcc9f9dfac9d458c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 34192023...; reboot acknowledged and connection reset observed; post-restart boot_id 2b968bb7... (changed); antrieb-links.service active, bonding/routes/forwarding restored, node3->node4 ping 0% loss\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart persistence and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5321cf3f28e04275\",\"cmd-c84e8e547a6d4f32\",\"cmd-a845d678442b41c1\",\"cmd-edefd7b799444835\",\"cmd-9102d6cf93334923\",\"cmd-2ec95846afa34ee0\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 8e8823ec...; reboot acknowledged, connection reset/timeout observed during restart; post-restart boot_id 0caec094... (changed); bonding/routes/forwarding restored, node4->node3 ping 0% loss (after transient neighbor-c
...[TRUNCATED 472 CHARACTERS]...
\":\"node4 restart persistence and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b1d9ef69ac23401e\",\"cmd-05324f61a5de4f47\",\"cmd-f4644d0fe1be4137\",\"cmd-dbbec60e09514a34\",\"cmd-046fd152f3724493\",\"cmd-1273dbc8ccd94c39\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 0581c914...; systemctl reboot acknowledged, connection timeout/reset observed; post-restart boot_id 547e58a1... (changed); enp8s0 static IP/route intact, ping to node3 0% loss\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final cross-cluster health confirmation after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-127d821edbcb4f76\",\"cmd-2e5328911ebb4cf6\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart-cycle check on node1 and node2 shows both bond0 slaves MII up and all required routes present on both nodes\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured redundant L3 connectivity between node1's private network (node3) and node2's private network (node4) carried over both independent node1-node2 links, with automatic failover and full node-restart persistence verified on all four nodes.\n\nTopology discovery: node1 eth1/eth2 and node2 eth1/eth2 are the two independent uplinks between node1-node2; node1 eth3 connects to node3's enp8s0, node2 eth3 connects to node4's enp8s0 (confirmed via targeted ping tests, since interfaces carried no IPs initially).\n\nImplementation:\n- node1: bond0 (Linux bonding, mode balance-rr, miimon 100) over eth1+eth2, IP 172.20.0.1/30 to node2; eth3 = 192.168.1.1/24 (node3's subnet). IP forwarding enabled globally and per-interface. Static route to 192.168.2.0/24 via bond0.\n- node2: mirrored — bond0 172.20.0.2/30, eth3 = 192.168.2.1/24 (node4's subnet), route to 192.168.1.0/24 via bond0.\n- node3/node4: enp8s0 statically addressed (192.168.1.2/24, 192.168.2.2/24) via existing NetworkManager profiles with a static route to the other private subnet via its local node1/node2 gateway — persists natively through NetworkManager.\n- Persistence on node1/node2: a systemd oneshot unit (antrieb-links.service, enabled, WantedBy=multi-user.target) reapplies the bonding/IP/forwarding/route configuration at boot, since SONiC's interfaces-config.service only manages eth0/lo and does not touch eth1-3.\n- Discovered and worked around a virtio/bonding limitation: 802.3ad (LACP) mode failed because virtio-net can't report link speed/duplex (dmesg: \"failed to get link speed/duplex\"), so switched to balance-rr, which works cleanly and actively load-balances across both links (confirmed via matched tx_packet counters growing symmetrically on eth1/eth2 for a test ping burst).\n- Also discovered that the platform's virtual point-to-point links do not propagate one-sided admin-down to the peer's carrier state (verified: bringing node1's eth1 down did not clear LOWER_UP on node2's eth1), so failover was correctly demonstrated as a full link outage (both endpoints down), which is the realistic failure model — 0% packet loss for node3↔node4 traffic in that state, and clean automatic recovery once both ends were restored.\n- Ran the mandatory node-restart protocol on all four nodes sequentially (one at a time, quorum/service preserved): captured pre-restart boot_id, restarted via `reboot`/`systemctl reboot`, polled until exec was available again, confirmed a new boot_id, and verified bonding/routes/forwarding/NetworkManager config and node3↔node4 connectivity recovered on each.","actions_performed":["Mapped node1/node2/node3/node4 interface topology via targeted temporary-IP ping tests since interfaces carried no addresses","Diagnosed and resolved a virtio-net + LACP (802.3ad) incompatibility, switching to balance-rr bonding","Configured bond0 (balance-rr, miimon 100) on node1 and node2 spanning both independent uplinks","Configured node1 eth3 (192.168.1.1/24) and node2 eth3 (192.168.2.1/24) as private-network gateways for node3/node4","Enabled global and per-interface IPv4 forwarding on node1 and node2","Added static routes on node1, node2, node3, node4 to reach the opposite private subnet","Persisted node3/node4 static addressing and routes via existing NetworkManager 'Wired connection 2' profiles","Created and enabled a systemd oneshot unit (antrieb-links.service) on node1 and node2 to reapply bonding/IP/forwarding/route config at boot","Verified active-active use of both links via symmetric tx_packet counters on eth1/eth2 during a ping burst","Disrupted link A (eth1) at both node1 and node2 to simulate a full link outage, confirmed 0% packet loss for node3<->node4 traffic, then restored and confirmed recovery and renewed dual-link usage","Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on node1, node2, node3, and node4 sequentially: captured baseline boot_id, restarted, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified recovered bonding/network/connectivity state"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Traffic between node3 and node4 private networks carried over both node1-node2 links (active-active)","command_ids":["cmd-0f843b275ff9425e","cmd-1252471645d7456b","cmd-c76cc7515bdd4590","cmd-610925e0415c4841","cmd-abd4b358ffe34674","cmd-f731b1ef61dd4c3c"],"summary":"bond0 (balance-rr) established on node1/node2 over eth1+eth2; node3->node4 ping succeeds; tx_packets on eth1 and eth2 both incremented by 23 during a 40-packet burst, proving both links carry traffic"},{"requirement":"node3/node4 keep reaching each other when either link is taken out of service","command_ids":["cmd-e4a7ab7dcedf406c","cmd-909eb0d3d5754798","cmd-c6a273fd271e4464","cmd-3e184f6642cd406f","cmd-aca6c570f9b849c8","cmd-5eb47c2c6e6b4c7a","cmd-c08de683c1294324","cmd-124486a0a16c4d4e","cmd-6ba16d7d0ffe445b","cmd-cae1127468c241b9","cmd-732ea34c97a245f5"],"summary":"Baseline 0% loss; link A (eth1) disabled at both endpoints (realistic full-link-outage model, since platform links don't propagate one-sided down); node3->node4 ping showed 0% loss over remaining link B; link A restored, bond returned to MII up on both slaves, and both links resumed carrying traffic evenly"},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-1fe7c86cc22a44f7","cmd-c116ca98add84f07","cmd-6a02d7168c6a48d9","cmd-d86b112ab0734c15","cmd-9d790d98a75e4e89","cmd-dcc9f9dfac9d458c"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 34192023...; reboot acknowledged and connection reset observed; post-restart boot_id 2b968bb7... (changed); antrieb-links.service active, bonding/routes/forwarding restored, node3->node4 ping 0% loss"},{"requirement":"node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-5321cf3f28e04275","cmd-c84e8e547a6d4f32","cmd-a845d678442b41c1","cmd-edefd7b799444835","cmd-9102d6cf93334923","cmd-2ec95846afa34ee0"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 8e8823ec...; reboot acknowledged, connection reset/timeout observed during restart; post-restart boot_id 0caec094... (changed); bonding/routes/forwarding restored, node4->node3 ping 0% loss (after transient neighbor-cache loss settled)"},{"requirement":"node3 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-5aa9009c030e4c5d","cmd-ab424fa1e3334dab","cmd-2a3c0819f06d480e","cmd-47089dac300840f4","cmd-e98fe19e63fb401b"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 83a0a80f...; systemctl reboot acknowledged, connection timeout/reset observed; post-restart boot_id a6e47589... (changed); NetworkManager-managed enp8s0 static IP/route intact, ping to node4 0% loss"},{"requirement":"node4 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-b1d9ef69ac23401e","cmd-05324f61a5de4f47","cmd-f4644d0fe1be4137","cmd-dbbec60e09514a34","cmd-046fd152f3724493","cmd-1273dbc8ccd94c39"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 0581c914...; systemctl reboot acknowledged, connection timeout/reset observed; post-restart boot_id 547e58a1... (changed); enp8s0 static IP/route intact, ping to node3 0% loss"},{"requirement":"Final cross-cluster health confirmation after all restarts","command_ids":["cmd-127d821edbcb4f76","cmd-2e5328911ebb4cf6"],"summary":"Post-restart-cycle check on node1 and node2 shows both bond0 slaves MII up and all required routes present on both nodes"}]},"ttft